@*
    Heroicons — the single icon source for the system.

    One catalog, one geometry (24x24, outline, 1.5 stroke), colour always
    inherited from context. That uniformity is most of what makes an icon
    set read as a set rather than as a collection.

    Accessibility follows use, not glyph. An icon sitting next to a visible
    label is decoration and is hidden from the accessibility tree, which is
    the default here. Pass Label only when the icon is the sole carrier of
    meaning — a standalone status mark, or an icon-only control whose own
    aria-label lives on the button rather than here.

        <Icon Name="users" />                       decorative, beside text
        <Icon Name="check-circle" Label="مُوثّق" /> meaningful on its own
        <Icon Name="trash" Size="sm" />             size step

    Reference: heroicons.com (v2, 24 outline).
*@

<svg class="hr-i @SizeClass @Class"
     viewBox="0 0 24 24"
     fill="none"
     stroke="currentColor"
     stroke-width="@StrokeWidth"
     stroke-linecap="round"
     stroke-linejoin="round"
     role="@(Label is null ? null : "img")"
     aria-hidden="@(Label is null ? "true" : null)"
     focusable="false"
     @attributes="Extra">
    @if (Label is not null)
    {
        <title>@Label</title>
    }
    @((MarkupString)Paths)
</svg>

